# React Query for API management

All server state must go through **React Query** (`react-query` v3). Do not fetch or mutate APIs with raw `useEffect` + Axios, ad-hoc `async` handlers that own loading/error state, or local `useState` as the source of truth for remote data.

## Stack

- Package: `react-query` (v3) — `QueryClient`, `QueryClientProvider`, `useQuery`, `useMutation`, `useQueryClient`
- HTTP client: Axios instance from `src/helpers/Api.js` (`api` default export / `BaseUrl`)
- Wrap the app with `QueryClientProvider` in `src/main.jsx` (keep it enabled)

## Rules

- **Reads** → `useQuery` (or `useInfiniteQuery` when paginating)
- **Writes** (create / update / delete) → `useMutation`
- Put `queryFn` / `mutationFn` on the Axios `api` helper — never `fetch` directly for backend calls
- Stable, descriptive `queryKey` arrays (e.g. `['users']`, `['products', id]`)
- After successful mutations, invalidate or update related queries via `queryClient.invalidateQueries`
- Prefer shared hooks under `src/hooks/` (or next to the feature) instead of inlining the same query in many pages
- Loading / error / success UI must use React Query status (`isLoading`, `isError`, `isSuccess`, `error`) — not parallel hand-rolled flags for the same request
- Show user-facing errors with Arabic toast/copy (react-toastify) when appropriate

## Patterns

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD — read
const { data, isLoading, isError } = useQuery(['users'], async () => {
  const { data } = await api.get('/users')
  return data
})

// ✅ GOOD — write + invalidate
const queryClient = useQueryClient()
const mutation = useMutation(
  (payload) => api.post('/users', payload),
  {
    onSuccess: () => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries(['users'])
    },
  }
)

// ❌ BAD — manual fetch as source of truth
useEffect(() => {
  api.get('/users').then((res) => setUsers(res.data))
}, [])
```

## Do not

- Call Axios in components without wrapping in `useQuery` / `useMutation`
- Duplicate loading/error state that React Query already provides
- Skip `QueryClientProvider` when adding new entry points
